==Strategy==
This stage is balanced around having at least two of the three [[Mysterious Force]]s maxed out; without them your [[Cat Cannon]] might not recharge fast enough to kill the Assassin Bears in time. If your Cannon Recharge + levels are too low, your Cannon also won't recharge fast enough, even with all three Mysterious Forces. Generally, you should only fire the Cannon when all three Bears are present on the screen. If needed, Cannon Recharge UP [[Cat Combo]]s may be used. It doesn't matter the size, one Small Cat Cannon Recharge UP Combo is all it takes, but more Combos do help.

:'''After three or four waves of Assassin Bears, you can expect the third Bear in each wave to be heavily delayed. To kill every third Bear without letting them push too much, save Sniper the Cat by disabling it seconds before it's about to fire and turn it back on after using the Cannon to kill the first two Bears.'''

Wall Doge has been buffed to where she can kill near anything in up to two hits, but when you consider her pitiful speed and range, this doesn't mean much. With a perfect spam of [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cats]], [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cats]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cats]], Wall Doge will barely advance on her own, and Sniper the Cat will negate any ground she regains. Another option is to weaken Wall Doge using [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] and bring a Unit Defense UP (Sm) combo. This allows a Lv.20+ Crazed Wall Cat to survive a hit from Wall Doge.

Then, either stack up cheap ranged damagers like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Leg Cats]], [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cats]] or heavy hitters like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Demon Cat]] to dish out damage to the boss. [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|Cats with knockback abilities]], like [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], can also do well at holding back the Wall Doge.

[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] is very useful on this stage, not only for holding off the Wall Doge, but also for briefly stalling the Assassin Bears until all three are on-screen so the Cannon can eliminate them. [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]] are another great option for stalling the Wall Doge, though they are far from necessary even on higher Crown difficulties. If you combine it with a [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attacker]] like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] or [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]], the stage can be cheesed.

[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] may serve as insurance should you fire the Cat Cannon too early, using the Wall Doge as a stepping stone to reach any remaining Assassin Bears.

A possible cheese strategy revolves around using Speed Combos, Tourist Cat, Gato Amigo and a Long-Distance cat like Courier Cat. Basically, save money until you can afford Tourist Cat, and after spawning him, spam Gato Amigo and occasionally Courier Cat. The idea is to knockback Wall Doge to the base so that Courier Cat can hit the base. Gato Amigo's Knockback [[Talents|Talent]] should be maxed before attempting this Cheese. Be warned that this strategy can be rather inconsistent.

